Circular ID: CIR-04 | Version: 1.0 | Effective: 2026-03-02 | Access: internal

Circular CIR-2026-005 (Document ID: CIR-04) establishes the updated mandatory=
 fallback procedure for retail financing applications when CTOS credit assess=
ment reports cannot be retrieved. Under this directive, applications encounte=
ring CTOS gateway downtime or retrieval errors must be placed in a system hol=
d status and re-queried after 4 hours. Automated system declines driven by bu=
reau unavailability or timeout are strictly prohibited.

1.0 - Purpose and Background
This Circular (CIR-2026-005) issues mandatory operational guidance regarding =
CTOS credit bureau retrieval failures. Effective 2026-03-02, all automated de=
cisioning engines and underwriting units within AEON Credit Service (M) Berha=
d must strictly adhere to the standardized fallback protocols defined herein,=
 superseding prior interim instructions.

2.0 - Scope of Application
This procedure governs all incoming retail credit and financing origination c=
hannels across all products offered by the Company, including AEON Classic Vi=
sa, AEON Gold Visa, AEON Platinum Visa, Personal Financing-i (Tawarruq), Moto=
rcycle Hire Purchase-i, Auto Hire Purchase-i, and Product (Objective) Financi=
ng.

3.0 - Detection of CTOS Service Disruption and System Hold Status
Upon encountering API timeout thresholds, connectivity disruptions, or bureau=
 maintenance responses during automated underwriting, the origination platfor=
m shall not terminate the application. The system must immediately assign the=
 status 'PENDING_BUREAU_RETRY' and hold the application in a paused operation=
al queue.

4.0 - Mandatory 4-Hour Retry Protocol
Applications placed on hold due to CTOS unavailability must undergo automated=
 retrieval retry attempts at fixed 4-hour intervals from the timestamp of the=
 initial failed query. The underwriting engine shall schedule subsequent poll=
ing up to a maximum of 3 consecutive automated cycles before rerouting to man=
ual queue processing.

5.0 - Prohibition of Automated Adverse Action
Under no circumstances shall the origination engine issue an automated reject=
ion or decline notice to an applicant due to bureau connection timeouts, thir=
d-party server errors, or incomplete CTOS data retrieval. Decisions must stri=
ctly be based on retrieved risk indicators (such as CTOS scores, bankruptcy i=
ndicators, legal action status, or active AKPK records) once successfully ret=
rieved.

6.0 - Escalation to Senior Underwriter Review
If the CTOS system remains unreachable after the secondary retry cycle (8 hou=
rs elapsed) or if persistent gateway faults are logged, the application file =
must be escalated directly to a Senior Underwriter. The Senior Underwriter ma=
y execute a secure web-portal retrieval, verify credit status via alternative=
 authorized interfaces, or hold the file pending bureau recovery.

7.0 - Customer Service and SLA Preservation
Operational teams must manage customer communication proactively. Where appli=
cants lodge status inquiries regarding held files, frontline teams must ackno=
wledge receipt within 2 business days. Applications delayed past 24 hours mus=
t be tracked under exception governance to avoid breach of standard turnaroun=
d commitments.
